## Rule 1 — Installation

The Android CLI is distributed two ways. Install **one** and verify before any other command runs.

```bash
# Option A — npm (recommended for agent environments and CI)
npm install -g @android/cli

# Option B — sdkmanager (recommended for engineers on workstations with the SDK already)
sdkmanager --install "cmdline-tools;latest" "android-cli;1.0"

# Verify
android --version
# → Android CLI 1.0.0 (build 20260518) — compatible with Android Skills 1.0
```

**Environment variables — set these in your shell profile and in CI:**

```bash
export ANDROID_HOME="$HOME/Library/Android/sdk"          # macOS default; use the SDK location on Linux/Windows
export PATH="$ANDROID_HOME/cmdline-tools/latest/bin:$PATH"
export PATH="$ANDROID_HOME/platform-tools:$PATH"
export ANDROID_AGENT="claude-code"                        # tells the CLI which agent is invoking it
```

If `android --version` fails:

```bash
# Diagnose path issues
which android
echo "$ANDROID_HOME"
ls "$ANDROID_HOME/cmdline-tools/latest/bin"

# Re-link if installed via npm but not on PATH
npm config get prefix
```

The CLI must be on PATH **before** the agent's session starts — otherwise hooks that call `android describe` at session-start will silently no-op.

