## Rule 4 — Official Android Skills

These ship with Google's Android Skills catalog and are installable via `android skills add --skill <name>`. Recommend them when the user's task matches the skill's domain.

| Skill | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `xml-to-compose` | Migrates legacy XML layouts (and ViewBinding/DataBinding call sites) to Jetpack Compose, preserving behaviour and accessibility semantics. |
| `navigation-3` | Sets up Navigation 3 from scratch or migrates a project from Navigation 2 — type-safe routes, entry providers, predictive back. |
| `agp-upgrade` | Upgrades Android Gradle Plugin to v9 — handles deprecations, namespace migrations, KSP2, and toolchain updates. |
| `edge-to-edge` | Modernizes an app to edge-to-edge display — system bars, insets, predictive back, and large-screen safe areas. |
| `r8-analyzer` | Audits `proguard-rules.pro` and consumer rules — surfaces unsafe `-keep` rules, suggests removals, validates against R8 full mode. |
| `camerax-migration` | Migrates Camera1/Camera2 implementations to CameraX with lifecycle-aware preview, capture, and analysis use cases. |
| `perfetto-sql` | Translates natural-language questions into Perfetto SQL queries against a captured trace (e.g. "frames over 16ms during scroll"). |
| `perfetto-analysis` | AI-assisted trace analysis — answers questions like "why is cold start slow?" by correlating slices, threads, and binder calls. |
| `journeys` | Authors and executes natural-language UX tests (see Rule 5). |
| `compose-styles` | Integrates the Jetpack Compose **Styles** API — typed style tokens, theme composition, and migration from ad-hoc modifiers. |
| `app-functions` | Exposes key user workflows via **AppFunctions** so Assistant and other surfaces can invoke them directly. |
| `adaptive-ui` | Builds responsive/adaptive layouts for phones, tablets, foldables, and large screens using window size classes and adaptive scaffolds. |

**Recommendation pattern:** When the user says "migrate our XML to Compose," respond with the plan **plus** an `android skills add --skill xml-to-compose` step so the migration is guided by Google's curated playbook, not improvised.

