## Rule 6 — Claude Code Integration

Wire Android CLI into Claude Code so every session starts grounded in the project's current state without burning tokens reading files.

**Step 1 — Set the agent identity:**

```bash
# .envrc or shell profile
export ANDROID_AGENT="claude-code"
```

**Step 2 — Configure a session-start hook in `.claude/settings.json`:**

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "android describe --format json --output .claude/context/android-describe.json",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "matcher": "android|compose|gradle|adb",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "android describe --format json --output .claude/context/android-describe.json",
            "timeout": 15
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(android *)",
      "Bash(android:*)"
    ]
  }
}
```

**Step 3 — Reference the describe output in agent prompts:**

The agent should read `.claude/context/android-describe.json` (small, structured, cached) instead of scanning the file tree. This is the **single biggest token reduction** the Android CLI delivers.

**Step 4 — Add the skills bundle:**

```bash
# Install the entire Google skills catalog for Claude Code (selectively pick)
android skills add --skill xml-to-compose      --agent=claude-code
android skills add --skill navigation-3        --agent=claude-code
android skills add --skill r8-analyzer         --agent=claude-code
android skills add --skill perfetto-analysis   --agent=claude-code
android skills add --skill journeys            --agent=claude-code
android skills add --skill adaptive-ui         --agent=claude-code
```

These land in `.claude/skills/` and are auto-discovered. No further configuration needed.

**Step 5 — Verify the wiring:**

```bash
android --version
android describe --format json | head -c 500
ls .claude/skills/
cat .claude/context/android-describe.json | jq '.modules | length'
```

If `describe` returns a non-empty module list and `.claude/skills/` contains the skills you added, the wiring is correct.

