## Rule 7 — CI Integration

Use Android CLI in GitHub Actions to keep CI deterministic, fast, and aligned with what agents run locally. **SHA-pin every third-party action** — same rule as the rest of the project.

```yaml
# .github/workflows/pr-check.yml
name: pr-check

on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  build-and-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 30
    steps:
      - name: Checkout
        uses: actions/checkout@692973e3d937129bcbf40652eb9f2f61becf3332  # v4.1.7

      - name: Set up JDK 17
        uses: actions/setup-java@99b8673ff64fbf99d8d325f52d9a5bdedb8483e9  # v4.2.1
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: '17'

      - name: Set up Gradle
        uses: gradle/actions/setup-gradle@db19848a5fa7950289d3668fb053140cf3028d43  # v3.3.2
        with:
          cache-encryption-key: ${{ secrets.GRADLE_ENCRYPTION_KEY }}

      - name: Install Android CLI
        run: |
          npm install -g @android/cli@1.0
          android --version

      - name: Describe project
        run: android describe --format json --output build/reports/describe.json

      - name: Build release
        run: android build --variant release --no-daemon

      - name: Unit + Compose tests
        run: android test --no-daemon

      - name: Instrumented tests
        run: android test --device emulator --avd pixel-8-api-35

      - name: Run smoke journeys
        run: android journeys run --tag smoke --format json --output build/reports/journeys.json

      - name: Upload reports
        if: always()
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@65462800fd760344b1a7b4382951275a0abb4808  # v4.3.3
        with:
          name: android-cli-reports
          path: build/reports/
          retention-days: 14
```

**Notes:**
- `android build --no-daemon` keeps each CI step isolated and matches the daemon-less mode Gradle Actions prefers.
- `android test --device emulator` provisions a managed AVD via `gradle-managed-devices` under the hood — no `reactivecircus/android-emulator-runner` required.
- Upload `describe.json` and `journeys.json` as artifacts so PR reviewers (human or AI) can ground their review without re-running the build.

